| `LoopbackMCPServer` `serverInfo.version` | `MailGentVersion.label` |

### README (required on every **ship**)

1. Headline → `**X.Y.Z alpha**`
2. **## Features** — fold every user-facing item from that version’s CHANGELOG into the matching subsection
3. Tool lists / Settings callouts / other README claims the release changed
4. Cross-check against CHANGELOG Added / Fixed / Changed / Breaking before closeout

## Git

- Do not land versioned work on `main` — branch `feat/…` / `fix/…` / `hotfix/…` first.
- Optional non-ship annotated tags `vX.Y.Z-rc.N` are allowed for dogfood bookmarks; they must **not** trigger Release / DMG as a ship. Prefer unsigned or clearly non-release; **ship tags** remain signed `vX.Y.Z` only.
- Docs/chore/internal-only: no version bump, no CHANGELOG entry.

## Signed release tags (required for ship)

GitHub **Verified** on the Tags page requires a cryptographically signed tag. Unsigned annotated tags and lightweight tags do **not** count.

**Always** create ship tags as:

```bash
    git tag -s "vX.Y.Z" -m "X.Y.Z alpha"
    git verify-tag "vX.Y.Z"   # must succeed before push
    git push origin "vX.Y.Z"
```

**Never** for a ship tag:

- `git tag vX.Y.Z` (lightweight)
- `git tag -a` without signing
- Tagging while `MailGentVersion.releaseCandidate > 0`
- Pushing a tag when `git verify-tag` fails
- Falling back to unsigned if signing is misconfigured — **stop** and fix signing first

### Signing setup (SSH preferred; one-time on this machine + GitHub)

If `git tag -s` fails with "gpg failed to sign the data", signing is not configured. Fix it before retrying.

1. `git config --global gpg.format ssh`
2. `git config --global user.signingkey ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_github` (or the key you use)
3. `git config --global gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile ~/.git_allowed_signers`
4. Create the allowed signers file with your email + public key:

   ```bash
   echo "$(git config user.email) $(cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_github.pub)" > ~/.git_allowed_signers
   ```

5. GitHub → Settings → SSH and GPG keys → **New SSH key** → Key type **Signing Key**
6. Optional: `git config --global tag.gpgsign true`

### Pre-tag checklist

```bash
    git config --get gpg.format
    git config --get user.signingkey
    git config --get gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile
    test -f "$(git config gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile)"
    # releaseCandidate must be 0 in MailGentVersion.swift / project.yml
```

Closeout must propose the signed form, e.g. `Proposed tag: git tag -s vX.Y.Z -m "X.Y.Z alpha"`.

## Tags vs GitHub Releases (alpha until v1)

| Surface | Format | Example |
|---------|--------|---------|
| Git ship tag | signed `vX.Y.Z` | `v0.24.1` |
| GitHub Release **title** | `X.Y.Z alpha` | `0.24.1 alpha` |
| GitHub **pre-release** | always checked | — |
| DMG filename | `MailGent-X.Y.Z.dmg` | `MailGent-0.24.1.dmg` |
| `MARKETING_VERSION` / bundle short version | `X.Y.Z` | `0.24.1` |
| Candidate display / MCP | `X.Y.Z-rc.N` | `0.24.1-rc.1` |

Workflow sets release title from the ship tag: strip leading `v`, append ` alpha`. Release notes start with every `CHANGELOG.md` section since the previous tag through this version (`Scripts/release/notes.sh`), then `.github/RELEASE_BODY.md`.

**Release-note images:** do **not** embed screenshots (e.g. `install-window.png`) in every release. Include an image only when that ship’s CHANGELOG window actually changed what the image shows (e.g. DMG install-guide layout → 0.23.5). `notes.sh` gates the DMG guide image on CHANGELOG keywords; keep `RELEASE_BODY.md` text-only for Install / Gatekeeper.

## Closeout

Every version / feature closeout report in chat **must** include a **Dogfood (mcp-tester)** section with visual **Do → Expect** scenarios for this change (UI labels, JSON statuses, Access Log chips). Point at `Scripts/mcp-tester/README.md`. See also `.cursor/rules/mcp-dogfood.mdc`.

**Default:** live MailGent + mcp-tester only. Do **not** include `fake_mailgent.py` / fake-harness steps in closeout unless the user asks for them. Do **not** write vague “run the shortcuts / expect it to work” dogfood.

**Layout:** keep the closeout / commit block in a fenced code box. Put **Dogfood (mcp-tester)** **outside** that box as normal chat markdown (scannable, copy-paste commands). Do not bury dogfood inside the commit-message fence.

### Candidate open / rc bump

```
Version closeout — X.Y.Z-rc.N (candidate)
Branch: feat/… or fix/…
Ship tag: none yet (releaseCandidate=N)

Proposed commit message:
<subject>

<body>

If you are happy with these changes, say so and I will stage and commit.
I will not commit until you confirm.
```

Then **outside** the fence (example shape — fill with this change’s real labels):

```
## Dogfood (mcp-tester)

**Setup:** MailGent running · `cd Scripts/mcp-tester && npm run tauri dev` · Connect `http://127.0.0.1:8788/mcp` + bearer

**Sanity:** …
**Scenario A — …**
- Do: …
- Expect: …
```

### Ship

```
Version closeout — vX.Y.Z
Branch: feat/… or fix/…
Proposed tag: git tag -s vX.Y.Z -m "X.Y.Z alpha"   # only when releaseCandidate=0

Proposed commit message:
<subject>

<body>

If you are happy with these changes, say so and I will stage and commit.
I will not commit until you confirm.
```

Then **outside** the fence: same **Dogfood (mcp-tester)** section.

Do not stage/commit/tag until the user confirms (unless they say **ship it**).

